WEBVTT

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:03.920
Hey, if you work in Claude,
Opencode, Cursor, Codex or just plain

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.256
live in the terminal, I’ve
got great news for you.

00:00:06.256 --> 00:00:10.552
Basecamp is coming to the command line and
the door is open for all your AI agents.

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:14.973
You can update projects, complete to dos,
make comments, even automate your entire

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:19.144
Basecamp routine, all with simple prompts
right from your terminal or agent.

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.687
You want to kick off
some work in Basecamp?

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:24.274
Just type in a quick prompt,
let the AI cook and boom!

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:25.775
There it is in Basecamp.

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:28.153
Or maybe you want
an automated announcement to Basecamp,

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:32.490
so tell it to do that, and once you're
done, it leaves a comment inside Basecamp.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.076
Wanna have your agent
actually work the bugs?

00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:38.705
Let it loose, then later
see what it did back on Basecamp.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.332
Whatever agent you

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:44.419
use, Basecamp is right there with you,
just on the command line.

00:00:44.502 --> 00:00:48.298
Now all the repos, examples and setup
instructions are linked on this page,

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:49.799
so grab those and get going.
